-- This file is hand-written. A signature install leaves it alone, so what is
-- put here is kept.
--
-- It is a stub: what stands here is a description of what belongs in it.
--
-- The side conditions of the correctness theorem: the predicates restricting a
-- proof to terms the semantics gives a meaning to, together with the `Decidable`
-- instances that decide them.
--
-- Both roles come from this one file on purpose. The conditions the rule proofs
-- assume and the conditions the executable checks at run time are then a single
-- definition, written down once, so the two cannot drift apart.
--
-- In Logos: `Cpc/Proofs/Assumptions.lean`.

